WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.890
With so many awesome Marvel movies and television
shows on the horizon, it can be hard to keep

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.500
up with the comic juggernaut's ever-growing
entertainment roster.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.480
Fear not: We're here to give you a glimpse
of all the upcoming Marvel projects outside

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.200
of and beyond the MCU's upcoming Phase 4.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.920
Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. has improved steadily
while seeming to perpetually be on the bubble;

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.200
it's been in real danger of cancellation by
ABC on multiple occasions, but has always

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.140
received a stay of execution from corporate
parent Disney.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:30.680
Season 5 ended on a note of relative finality,
so it surprised pretty much everyone when

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.640
the show was re-upped not only for a sixth
season, but a seventh.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.160
It was, in fact, the very first series to
be slotted by the network for 2020.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:43.510
At San Diego Comic-Con in July 2019, Marvel
TV head Jeph Loeb confirmed that the seventh

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.880
season would be the last.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:49.670
Both seasons would be slightly truncated,
featuring 13 episodes as opposed to the standard

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.360
22 of previous seasons.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.680
In the interest of forging a lean and mean
narrative, Season 6 has chosen to forgo any

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.940
reference to the larger Marvel Cinematic Universe,
up to and including the world-changing events

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:05.140
of Avengers: Infinity War and Avengers: Endgame,
to focus on telling its own story.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.430
The season has focused on the organization's
rebuilding period under new leadership, as

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:14.050
Phil Coulson was confirmed to have died shortly
after the events of Season 5, but this rebuilding

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:18.310
is disrupted by the appearance of mysterious,
interdimensional hostiles led by a man who

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:20.200
happens to looks exactly like Coulson.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.860
It seems certain that S.H.I.E.L.D.'s writers
already have a pretty good idea how it will

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:27.700
all play out going into next year's seventh
season, but as for the rest of us, we'll just

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.720
have to wait to find out.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:34.200
The SUMC, or Sony Universe of Marvel Characters,
if you're not into the whole brevity thing,

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.229
was born of Sony Pictures' deal with Marvel
Studios, which allowed Marvel to integrate

00:01:38.229 --> 00:01:39.680
Spider-Man into the MCU.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.620
In exchange, Sony continues to produce ol'
Web-head's MCU-set solo outings, and also

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.460
has free rein to develop its own universe
based on ancillary Spider-Man characters.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:53.640
This universe's inaugural effort, 2018's Venom,
cleaned up at the box office while satisfying

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:58.150
fans of the character left cold by Topher
Grace's unfortunate portrayal in Sam Raimi's

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.080
Spider-Man 3.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.800
After that somewhat unexpected success, Sony
was quick to fast-track another Spidey-related

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.580
property that had been gestating since 2017.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.239
That would be Morbius, based on the "living
vampire" and frequent Spider-Man nemesis who

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.360
first appeared in the pages of Marvel comics
in 1971.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:19.360
The flick will star Jared Leto as Dr. Michael
Morbius, a brilliant biochemist whose attempts

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:23.579
to cure his own potentially fatal blood disease
with an experimental treatment, involving

00:02:23.579 --> 00:02:27.849
the blood of vampire bats, go predictably
awry, transforming him into a superpowered

00:02:27.849 --> 00:02:30.140
ghoul who must consume human blood to survive.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:35.200
Daniel Espinosa directs from a script by Lost
in Space co-creators Matt Sazama and Burk

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:35.700
Sharpless.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:40.420
We'll see if the SUMC can establish a dark,
horror-tinged streak when the movie hits screens

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.170
on July 31, 2020.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:47.689
While nearly all of the upcoming Marvel projects
presented at SDCC had either long been rumored

00:02:47.689 --> 00:02:51.560
or actually confirmed, there was a single
outlier that came as a complete shock to the

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:52.060
crowd.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:57.140
To conclude the panel, Kevin Feige presented
two-time Academy Award winning actor Mahershala

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:01.200
Ali, whose scintillating performance as the
villain Cottonmouth was the best part of the

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.720
Marvel Netflix series Luke Cage.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:07.739
Feige then announced that Ali would star in
the title role in an MCU incarnation of Blade,

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.150
and jaws throughout Hall H could be heard
hitting the floor as far away as L.A.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:12.820
"What is that?"

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.579
The first movie adaptation of Blade, released
in 1998 and starring Wesley Snipes as the

00:03:21.579 --> 00:03:26.109
half human-half vampire hero, is sometimes
considered to be the first modern superhero

00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:26.600
film.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.439
The flick spawned two sequels, and for virtually
the entire existence of the MCU, fans have

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.340
been wondering if the "Daywalker" would ever
get his time to shine in the MCU.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:39.820
Feige put that speculation to rest in dramatic
fashion, and the involvement of the immensely

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.860
talented Ali is nothing short of a coup.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:47.059
No further casting or plot details were announced,
but there is one bit of bad news: Feige confirmed

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.980
that Blade will not hit screens until the
MCU's Phase 5.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:53.220
Call it the great Gunn-troversy of 2018.

00:03:53.529 --> 00:03:57.559
In July of that year, the news broke that
James Gunn, writer and director of the beloved

00:03:57.559 --> 00:04:01.510
Guardians of the Galaxy franchise, had been
let go from the third installment over a series

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.459
of old tweets that had been dug up by conservative
pundits.

00:04:04.459 --> 00:04:08.669
Guardians fans were up in arms, but a silver
lining came in August, when it was announced

00:04:08.669 --> 00:04:10.699
that Gunn's completed script would be used.

00:04:10.699 --> 00:04:15.599
The search was on for a new director, a search
that continued right up until March of 2019,

00:04:15.599 --> 00:04:19.410
when Disney put an end to the whole kerfuffle
by seemingly saying "the hell with it" and

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:20.220
re-hiring Gunn.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:24.400
The nearly year-long impasse will have the
effect of delaying Vol. 3 for a bit, as it

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.940
didn't take Gunn long after his canning to
find another gig, at rival Warner Bros., writing

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:31.680
and directing a reimagined Suicide Squad for
DC.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:36.080
Marvel Studios has agreed to wait patiently
until Gunn's work on that film, which is slotted

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:41.100
for release in the summer of 2021, is done
before putting Vol. 3 into production, meaning

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.520
that we're not likely to see it hit the big
screen until at least 2022.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:48.440
Marvel isn't playing coy about King T'Challa's
second solo outing.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.700
It doesn't have an official title or release
date, but Black Panther 2 has been officially

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:57.169
confirmed by the studio, not exactly a huge
surprise, as the original became one of the

00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:02.320
highest-grossing films of all time and Marvel's
first to receive serious Oscar consideration,

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.940
winning three for its original score, costume
design, and production design.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:10.200
Not only is the sequel officially happening,
but Feige revealed to Entertainment Weekly

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.610
that the concept is already coming together
nicely.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:13.610
He told EW:

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:17.940
"One of the favorite pastimes at Marvel Studios
is sitting around on a Part One and talking

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.120
and dreaming about what we would do in a Part
Two.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.960
There have been plenty of those conversations
as we were putting together the first Black

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:24.460
Panther.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:28.960
We have ideas and a pretty solid direction
on where we want to head with the second one."

00:05:28.979 --> 00:05:32.870
Writer/director Ryan Coogler is officially
on board, and while nothing is confirmed,

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:37.500
it's expected that the principal cast, including
Chadwick Boseman, Lupita Nyong'O and Danai

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.060
Gurira, will also return.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:44.060
It's even been rumored that Michael B. Jordan's
Erik Killmonger could return in some capacity,

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:47.360
despite being left in no condition to do so
at the end of Black Panther.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.160
In light of the megabucks that film made,
we're likely to get additional details on

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:54.160
this highly-anticipated sequel sooner rather
than later.

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:58.200
Given the fact that it kicked off a universe
of Spider-Man characters which will not, so

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:02.400
far as we now know, actually feature Spider-Man,
the success of Sony's Venom was a bit of a

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:02.900
shock.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:07.180
Anchored by Tom Hardy's completely bonkers
performance, the film cleaned up at the worldwide

00:06:07.189 --> 00:06:12.370
box office of the tune of $855 million, making
a sequel inevitable.

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:16.160
Of course, having learned a few tricks from
Marvel Studios, Sony made sure to go ahead

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:20.650
and set one up in advance with a post-credits
scene featuring Woody Harrelson as Cletus

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:24.500
Kasady, the psychopathic serial killer who
will go on to bond with Carnage, the Venom

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.680
symbiote's offspring.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:30.500
Venom 2 was at one time assumed to be the
"Untitled Sony/Marvel sequel" which the studio

00:06:30.509 --> 00:06:34.669
had slotted for an October 2020 release, but
that is no longer set in stone due to the

00:06:34.669 --> 00:06:39.130
departure of Venom director Ruben Fleischer,
who has his hands full with the long-awaited

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.760
sequel to his 2009 classic Zombieland.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:46.180
But the second go-round for the Lethal Protector
is still in active development, with original

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:51.069
scribe Kelly Marcel already drafting a screenplay,
and Hardy set to return along with co-star

00:06:51.069 --> 00:06:52.240
Michelle Williams.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.979
Plot details are sketchy, but one thing is
certain: just as Kasady promised in that stinger…

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:04.099
"When I get outta here, and I will, there's
gonna be Carnage."

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:09.480
…Variety confirmed in January 2019 that
Harrelson's murderous symbiote will be Venom

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:10.340
2's main villain.

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:14.860
It's a little tough to believe that at this
point, Spider-Man has a rich cinematic history

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:19.160
spanning almost 20 years and nearly a dozen
feature films, yet here we are.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:23.960
For all the box office bucks raked in by Sam
Raimi's trilogy, the Amazing Spider-Man reboot

00:07:23.969 --> 00:07:28.870
series, and the MCU iteration ably portrayed
by Tom Holland, none of those films were able

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:32.919
to do what Sony Pictures Animation's Spider-Man:
Into the Spider-Verse did: score an Academy

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:33.420
Award.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:38.639
2018's Best Animated Feature winner is considered
by some to be among the best, if not the best,

00:07:38.639 --> 00:07:43.039
superhero films ever made, with its supremely
innovative animation style and focus on its

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.400
eclectic cast of alternate-universe Spider-People.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:49.319
It's so singular a cinematic achievement that
it seems like its success would be impossible

00:07:49.319 --> 00:07:52.529
to duplicate, but darned if Sony isn't going
to try.

00:07:52.529 --> 00:07:56.379
The Spider-Verse sequel will center on the
burgeoning romantic relationship between Miles

00:07:56.379 --> 00:08:01.760
Morales and Gwen Stacy, a.k.a. Ghost-Spider,
and, according to co-director Rodney Rothman,

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:05.039
will take place two years after the events
of the first film.

00:08:05.039 --> 00:08:09.419
Additional plot details are still a mystery,
but Sony Pictures' Amy Pascal has let slip

00:08:09.419 --> 00:08:13.820
that the sequel will feature even more female
versions of Spidey besides Gwen Stacy and

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:14.600
Peni Parker.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.940
In fact, it will serve to set up a spin-off
film focused entirely on these characters

00:08:18.949 --> 00:08:23.009
in the form of a similarly animated film that
will introduce classic Spider-Woman Jessica

00:08:23.009 --> 00:08:25.940
Drew along with Cindy Moon, also known as
Silk.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:31.719
Disney's acquisition of Fox gave the House
of Mouse a 60% stake in Hulu, and even before

00:08:31.719 --> 00:08:35.480
the deal closed, the streamer was looking
to expand its Marvel offerings beyond its

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.200
hit original series Runaways.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:42.020
The first set of announced new projects, however,
came as a bit of a surprise: four adult animated

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:46.590
series centered on some of the quirkier characters
in Marvel lore, which will, of course, cross

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:47.980
over for a team-up special.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:53.460
All co-produced by TV EVP Jeph Loeb, each
series features creative talent just as eclectic

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:54.840
as the characters themselves.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:09:00.120
Get ready for: The Tigra and Dazzler Show,
produced by Chelsea Handler; Hit-Monkey, courtesy

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:04.370
of Blades of Glory writing team Josh Gordon
and Will Speck; M.O.D.O.K., which will be

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:07.300
written and produced by Patton Oswalt; and,
wait for it…

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:09.840
"What do you let him lick you like that for?

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:12.400
Gross."

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:16.720
That's right!

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.280
Kevin Smith will be helming Howard the Duck.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:22.320
Obviously, each series looks to be aiming
for its own distinct comedic vibe, but Loeb

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:26.160
will be tasked with bringing them all together
for The Offenders, a one-off special in which

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:29.940
all of these weird characters will team up
to tackle a common enemy which threatens the

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:30.440
world.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:35.040
Marvel's first foray into animated comedy
looks interesting, to say the least, and finally,

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.920
we'll hopefully get a version of Howard the
Duck to once and for all purge the memory

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:41.680
of that terrible, terrible 1986 film.

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:47.320
"Now, you and Baby Face are going to beat
it, right, Mr. Zits?

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.900
Before I get really mad!"

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:55.500
While a sequel to the billion-dollar-plus
grossing Captain Marvel seems like a foregone

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.640
conclusion, it has also yet to be confirmed.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.260
According to leaker extraordinaire "Wardell,"
the wheels are turning.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:05.720
Star Brie Larson is reported to have signed
a seven-picture deal with Marvel, and it sure

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:09.530
seems unlikely that the studio's brass would
be content to simply have Carol Danvers pop

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:13.870
up in other characters' movies after her first
solo vehicle's stellar box office performance.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:18.090
Interestingly, "Wardell" isn't the only leaker
to have claimed inside knowledge about Captain

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:18.800
Marvel 2.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:23.820
A Redditor posting under the name TheMarvelScoopMaster
asserted that the sequel will take place during

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:28.350
Avengers: Endgame's five-year time jump, and
will see Carol Danvers tangle with the interdimensional

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:33.790
cyborg Michael Korvac, a character with a
history in the comics stretching back to 1975,

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:36.690
who had dealings with the likes of the Grandmaster
and Doctor Strange.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:41.230
The Redditor claims that Danvers will investigate
a Kree "secret weapon" that turns out to be

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:45.630
Korvac, and that the two will initially bond
over having both been unwilling Kree experiments.

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:49.380
But then, Korvac will betray Danvers, and
the two will end up doing battle in the film's

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:49.880
climax.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:54.280
Of course, this is merely an unsubstantiated
rumor, so be sure to take it with a grain

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:54.780
of salt.

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.800
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:01.100
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:05.320
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

